Sync encrypted .env files with evnx cloud.

Secrets are encrypted on this machine before upload. The server stores
ciphertext and cannot read them.

A failed request to the server has its own exit code (10-15), the same
for `evnx auth`, `evnx vault` and `evnx org`; `evnx cloud run` returns the
command's own code once it has started. See the table below.

TLS: evnx trusts its bundled root certificates plus any in the PEM
bundle named by SSL_CERT_FILE or the directory named by SSL_CERT_DIR
(files ending .pem or .crt, or hashed names like a1b2c3d4.0). Behind a
TLS-inspecting proxy, set SSL_CERT_FILE to your organisation's CA
bundle. A variable that names a missing path or a file with no
certificate is an error, exit 13.

Usage: evnx cloud [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  push            Encrypt a .env and upload it as a new version
  pull            Download a version and decrypt it
  run             Run a command with a vault's variables in its environment
  history         List a vault's versions, newest first
  watch           Watch a vault and report when someone pushes a new version
  diff            What changed between two versions — key names only, never values
  audit           Who did what to a vault, newest first
  delete-version  Delete one version of a vault, and its encrypted blob
  link            Bind this directory to a vault, so push and pull need no --vault
  unlink          Remove this directory's vault binding
  export          Write a vault's secrets to a directory, decrypted — the way out
  status          Show whether this machine is set up for cloud sync
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --server <URL>
          evnx server to talk to. Overrides EVNX_SERVER and config.toml.
          
          Plain http:// is refused for anything but a loopback address, because the access and refresh tokens travel in request headers.

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes:
    0  Ran, nothing to report
    1  Ran, and found something: findings, problems, a difference, not in sync
    2  Could not run: usage, config, I/O, or refused before any change
    4  Declined: answered no, or a confirmation was needed with no terminal and no --yes
   10  Not signed in, or the token was rejected
   11  Forbidden, or the email is not verified
   12  The plan's limit is reached
   13  Server unreachable, not an evnx server, or TLS roots unusable
   14  Conflict, or locked
   15  Server error, or rate limited
  141  Output closed early (broken pipe)
    N  Once the command has started: its own exit code, or 128+n if signal n killed it

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/cloud
